as refused before start because the door takes the token `sonnet`, not `claude-sonnet-5-5`. It was relaunched with `sonnet`, the same model and family. The what is settled.\n\nFindings:\n1. correctness \u00b7 verifiable: \u00b7 scripts/forge.py:64 (`NET_ERR`) \u00b7 blocking.\n   - `could not resolve` also matches gh's not-found error. Evidence: `gh pr view 999999` prints `GraphQL: Could not resolve to a PullRequest with the number of 999999.` and `forge.NET_ERR.search` returns True on it.\n   - scenario: a mistyped or deleted PR number given to gaze, verify-gate or `forge.py resolve` raises ForgeUnreachable and writes the 300 s offline mark to the clone-wide `idh-forge-cache.json`. For the next 5 minutes, every review of every other cached PR in that clone (parallel raid waves included) skips `git fetch` and takes its head from a possibly stale `origin/<branch>`. Discussion and CI go unread. `review_evidence.py forge` on a missing PR exits 4 (proceed, unread) instead of 3 (Missing Data).\n   - on main: no. Base 52404e5b has no offline mark, so a missing PR fails `cannot read PR` and affects nothing else.\n   - fix: narrow the pattern to host-level errors (`could not resolve host`), and add a test with the GraphQL not-found stderr.\n2. redteam \u00b7 consider: \u00b7 scripts/forge.py:240-252 \u00b7 `_cached` takes the head from `refs/remotes/origin/<branch>` and caches no head-repository identity, so a fork PR whose branch name collides with an origin branch would map to the wrong commit offline. This is downgraded from the seat's blocking: there are 0 cross-repository PRs in the last 300 of this repo, so no real actor produces it today. It matters for an adopter that takes fork PRs.\n3. redteam \u00b7 consider: \u00b7 scripts/forge.py:294, scripts/raid_land.py:228 \u00b7 a thread's time is its latest comment's `createdAt`. A thread reopened, or a comment edited, after the gate's read with no new comment falls outside the landing window.\n4. correctness \u00b7 consider: \u00b7 scripts/forge.py `_load_cache`/`_save_cache` \u00b7 read-modify-write without a lock. Concurrent gazes can drop each other's `prs` entry, which fails closed (\"never resolved\").\n5. correctness \u00b7 consider: \u00b7 scripts/forge.py:196 \u00b7 the offline mark also short-circuits non-read calls (strict pointer comments) for 300 s after one read timeout. This is per design, noted.\nnofollow: second-resolution `forge_read` against strict `>` (the stamp is taken before the query, so it is conservative). The `gate_read` fallback to a verdict on another head is guarded by `check_head`.\n\nExit criteria (code reading by two seats, tests run): (1) cached PR offline completes, unread stated: met, tests/test_forge_offline.py. (2) First-ever offline review stops with a clear message: met. (3) Landing refuses on a newer unresolved review: met, tests/test_raid_land.py. (4) Skill texts updated: met. `make check` was not run here.\nTargeted tests: selected: 19 files (test_forge*, test_gaze_*, test_raid_land*, test_review_evidence, ...); fallback: none; result: pass (19 selected file(s)), 424 passed.\n\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 4m06s\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=2 tokens=na cost~=$na\nseat: correctness \u00b7 runtime=claude \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=claude-sonnet-5-5 \u00b7 model=claude-sonnet-5-5 \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: redteam \u00b7 runtime=codex \u00b7 family=openai \u00b7 route=gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 model=openai/gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 status: ran\n"}

